WEBVTT

﻿1

00:03:21.702 --> 00:03:23.244
Hey, how did you open your cell door?


00:03:23.912 --> 00:03:24.871
Hey!


00:03:24.955 --> 00:03:25.955
What are you doing?


00:03:26.707 --> 00:03:27.707
Open Sector 2!


00:03:30.294 --> 00:03:31.294
How did you get out?


00:03:33.297 --> 00:03:34.630
Get back in your cell.


00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:37.925
I told you, get back in your cell!


00:03:38.468 --> 00:03:40.511
Let's give you a few friends to play with.


00:03:54.318 --> 00:03:55.526
Sorry.


00:04:02.659 --> 00:04:03.659
Send some guards in.


00:04:03.744 --> 00:04:04.744
I'm trying.


00:04:11.376 --> 00:04:13.336
Okay, I'm set.
How's things going down below?


00:04:13.503 --> 00:04:15.254
How do you think? I'm in a sewer.


00:04:15.589 --> 00:04:17.548
The doors won't open! We're locked in!


00:04:18.216 --> 00:04:19.216
Sound the alarm!


00:04:27.851 --> 00:04:28.935
We've lost control!


00:04:29.645 --> 00:04:30.645
Captain!


00:04:46.203 --> 00:04:47.870
I'm in position.


00:04:48.872 --> 00:04:50.039
Move to phase 2.


00:05:43.844 --> 00:05:45.511
What are you doing?
What are you doing?


00:05:45.637 --> 00:05:47.430
What's wrong?
What's happening, Benji?


00:05:47.514 --> 00:05:49.140
Oh, God.
He's not going to the extraction point.


00:05:49.266 --> 00:05:51.434
Stay focused.
He knows where he's going.


00:05:58.817 --> 00:06:01.944
No, I'm not. I won't.
I will not open that door.


00:06:02.029 --> 00:06:05.281
Please go to the extraction point, Ethan.
I know.


00:06:05.365 --> 00:06:08.117
I know what this means, but I can't.
I'm not authorized...


00:06:09.619 --> 00:06:11.287
Go to the extraction point, Ethan.


00:06:11.455 --> 00:06:12.955
Go to the extraction point!


00:06:13.540 --> 00:06:15.166
Oh, you're just going to wait.


00:06:15.292 --> 00:06:17.334
We're going to wait. Great. I can wait.


00:06:27.471 --> 00:06:29.472
Okay, fine. Fine! Fine!


00:06:29.931 --> 00:06:31.015
There.


00:06:31.099 --> 00:06:33.726
We'll just screw
the whole thing up on purpose.


00:06:39.566 --> 00:06:42.318
Jane? We're going
to have a slight delay.


00:07:00.670 --> 00:07:03.297
Why do you want to go in there?


00:07:09.805 --> 00:07:12.932
Bogdan!


00:07:14.684 --> 00:07:15.684
Sergei?


00:07:16.103 --> 00:07:17.103
Time to go!


00:07:17.687 --> 00:07:18.687
Now?


00:07:19.064 --> 00:07:20.064
Yes, now!


00:07:23.693 --> 00:07:26.362
I don't know what he's doing,
and for some reason, I'm helping him.


00:07:26.530 --> 00:07:28.781
As long as he's where he should be
when the song ends.


00:07:32.786 --> 00:07:35.079
We have a passenger.


00:08:01.773 --> 00:08:02.898
Sergei!


00:08:13.410 --> 00:08:15.077
Open all of them!


00:08:33.513 --> 00:08:34.513
Oh God!


00:08:35.265 --> 00:08:38.142
Oh God oh God oh God. ..


00:08:38.560 --> 00:08:42.104
Sergei, please tell me there's more to this plan!


00:09:20.977 --> 00:09:21.977
Let's go. ..


00:09:22.145 --> 00:09:23.395
Agent Hunt?


00:09:23.480 --> 00:09:24.480
And you are?


00:09:25.148 --> 00:09:26.232
Agent Carter.


00:09:26.983 --> 00:09:28.067
Okay.


00:09:29.861 --> 00:09:30.945
Who's your pal?


00:09:31.029 --> 00:09:32.238
I'll tell you on the way!


00:09:36.618 --> 00:09:38.035
Light the fuse.


00:11:37.197 --> 00:11:38.864
Sergei, what's going on?


00:11:38.948 --> 00:11:39.948
It's OK, Bogdan.


00:11:40.033 --> 00:11:41.909
I don't mean to bring up
the elephant in the room,


00:11:41.993 --> 00:11:43.786
but what's with the big, hairy Russian?


00:11:43.953 --> 00:11:47.122
Who, Bogdan? He fed me intel. If I left
him there, they would've killed him.


00:11:47.290 --> 00:11:48.707
So we're gonna give him his freedom.


00:11:48.792 --> 00:11:49.875
Did you call in the sweepers?


00:11:49.959 --> 00:11:50.959
On their way.


00:11:51.044 --> 00:11:52.795
Good, good.


00:11:54.297 --> 00:11:56.882
Benji, how is it you're here?


00:11:57.300 --> 00:11:59.009
Oh, I passed the field exam.


00:11:59.636 --> 00:12:01.136
Crazy, right?


00:12:01.638 --> 00:12:03.180
Yeah. Crazy.


00:12:03.306 --> 00:12:04.890
- DNA test.
- It's me.


00:12:04.974 --> 00:12:06.809
It's procedure.
I'm just confirming it's you.


00:12:06.893 --> 00:12:08.727
- You're very thorough.
- Sergei?


00:12:08.812 --> 00:12:10.145
Are you not Russian?


00:12:10.730 --> 00:12:11.772
Relax.


00:12:12.315 --> 00:12:14.316
Sweepers approaching! Brooms are out!


00:12:14.401 --> 00:12:15.901
- Roger that.
- Sergei.


00:12:17.070 --> 00:12:19.363
Are you not Sergei?


00:12:24.160 --> 00:12:25.577
You'll be fine.


00:12:25.703 --> 00:12:26.912
Bogdan.


00:12:27.038 --> 00:12:28.455
I always take care of my friends.


00:12:28.581 --> 00:12:30.499
My friend.


00:12:36.798 --> 00:12:38.257
Messy bringing him along.


00:12:38.425 --> 00:12:39.925
I thought it went rather well.


00:12:40.051 --> 00:12:42.010
Mind telling me what you were doing
in a Russian prison?


00:12:42.137 --> 00:12:43.971
Mind telling me why you broke me out?


00:12:45.473 --> 00:12:47.349
This wasn't a rescue mission?


00:12:47.434 --> 00:12:48.976
Let me put it this way.


00:12:49.060 --> 00:12:51.728
If the Secretary wanted me out of there,


00:12:52.897 --> 00:12:54.857
it must be pretty bad out here.


00:12:58.153 --> 00:12:59.653
We were after a file.


00:13:00.405 --> 00:13:01.697
We lost it.


00:13:01.823 --> 00:13:04.324
"We"? Who lost it? You?


00:13:09.873 --> 00:13:11.039
Agent Hanaway.


00:13:11.499 --> 00:13:12.749
Where's Hanaway?


00:13:22.886 --> 00:13:25.179
It was a letter drop.


00:13:25.263 --> 00:13:26.930
Classified file.


00:13:27.348 --> 00:13:29.600
It should have been a simple intercept.


00:13:37.942 --> 00:13:39.902
We knew which train
the courier was on.


00:13:39.986 --> 00:13:41.820
ETA, two minutes on the courier.


00:13:41.905 --> 00:13:43.363
But there was one thing we didn't know.


00:13:43.448 --> 00:13:45.657
Bobcat, your train's six minutes out.


00:13:45.783 --> 00:13:46.909
Who the courier was.


00:14:00.882 --> 00:14:02.341
It's now or never, Bobcat.


00:14:03.218 --> 00:14:06.595
The courier delivering the file,
what's his name?


00:14:06.679 --> 00:14:08.222
Go ahead. Shoot.


00:14:08.348 --> 00:14:10.224
We are out of time.


00:14:16.105 --> 00:14:19.399
I need a name, folks.
I can't track all these people at once.


00:14:20.693 --> 00:14:24.071
Marek. Stefanski. For the love of God!


00:14:24.197 --> 00:14:25.197
You got it?


00:14:25.406 --> 00:14:27.324
Marek Stefanski.


00:14:29.953 --> 00:14:30.953
Searching.


00:14:44.342 --> 00:14:46.176
I'll take it from here.


00:14:56.020 --> 00:14:57.854
Hey, you all right, buddy?


00:14:57.939 --> 00:15:00.065
Hanaway dropped the mark
and grabbed his bag.


00:15:00.149 --> 00:15:02.651
Sit down. Catch your breath.


00:15:04.028 --> 00:15:07.573
He had the file in his hands.
Easy in, easy out.


00:15:07.699 --> 00:15:08.699
File secured.


00:15:10.368 --> 00:15:13.287
But we weren't the only ones after it.


00:15:13.371 --> 00:15:16.290
Bobcat, someone else
has crashed this party.


00:15:18.209 --> 00:15:19.501
I'm not alone.


00:15:20.503 --> 00:15:21.587
Local police?


00:15:21.671 --> 00:15:23.880
No. Armed hostiles.


00:15:31.264 --> 00:15:34.057
Hang tight, I'm coming!
Outrigger, back him up.


00:15:34.684 --> 00:15:35.976
Negative, Outrigger.


00:15:36.060 --> 00:15:38.478
Rendezvous southwest corner,
60 seconds.


00:15:40.356 --> 00:15:43.609
Hanaway's lens cam drew a facial
match and triggered a warning.


00:15:46.738 --> 00:15:48.113
But it was too late.


00:15:55.246 --> 00:15:56.413
No!


00:16:01.085 --> 00:16:02.711
You're going to be okay.


00:16:06.382 --> 00:16:07.883
You're so beautiful.


00:16:09.677 --> 00:16:13.055
I'm sorry, I. .. I should have told you.


00:16:17.769 --> 00:16:19.394
It was my op.


00:16:21.064 --> 00:16:22.898
I put him in the field.


00:16:23.733 --> 00:16:26.777
And she left him
just alive enough for me to see him die.


00:16:44.420 --> 00:16:45.587
I'm sorry.


00:16:48.925 --> 00:16:49.925
You know her?


00:16:50.551 --> 00:16:53.053
That's Sabine Moreau. Contract killer.


00:16:54.097 --> 00:16:55.764
Works for diamonds.


00:16:56.974 --> 00:16:58.266
What was in the file?


00:17:06.526 --> 00:17:08.402
Russian nuclear launch codes.


00:17:16.327 --> 00:17:20.080
IMF's been looking for an emerging
extremist, code name, Cobalt.


00:17:20.164 --> 00:17:23.291
He's determined to detonate
a nuclear weapon however he can.


00:17:23.376 --> 00:17:25.544
We know Moreau's
worked for him before.


00:17:25.628 --> 00:17:27.796
What else does IMF know about him?


00:17:28.965 --> 00:17:30.298
As much as you do now.


00:17:30.675 --> 00:17:32.426
But if Moreau has nuclear launch codes,


00:17:32.510 --> 00:17:35.137
you can bet Cobalt's gone
from a person of interest


00:17:35.221 --> 00:17:36.638
to enemy number one.


00:17:37.557 --> 00:17:38.640
We're here.


00:18:02.165 --> 00:18:03.498
Agent confirmed.


00:18:03.833 --> 00:18:05.667
Why was he in prison?


00:18:06.669 --> 00:18:10.464
He disappeared after he and his wife...
You know.


00:18:11.549 --> 00:18:14.634
I thought he'd just been transferred.
Put on leave.


00:18:15.678 --> 00:18:19.765
There were rumors, though.
Talk of an unsanctioned hit.


00:18:19.849 --> 00:18:21.433
Welcome back, Mr. Hunt.


00:18:21.517 --> 00:18:24.770
In your absence,
IMF has learned that Cobalt is or was


00:18:24.854 --> 00:18:27.564
a level-1 nuclear strategist
for Russian intelligence.


00:18:27.648 --> 00:18:30.776
Therefore, the only way to uncover
his actual identity


00:18:30.860 --> 00:18:33.153
is to infiltrate the Kremlin itself.


00:18:33.988 --> 00:18:35.614
In order to get past their checkpoints,


00:18:35.698 --> 00:18:38.617
you'll be impersonating
General Anatoly Fedorov.


00:18:38.701 --> 00:18:40.660
We believe Cobalt
will do everything he can


00:18:40.745 --> 00:18:42.746
to destroy any record of his identity.


00:18:42.830 --> 00:18:44.915
Your mission,
should you choose to accept it,


00:18:45.041 --> 00:18:48.126
is to penetrate the highly-secured
archive inside the Kremlin


00:18:48.211 --> 00:18:50.420
and retrieve Cobalt's file
before he can destroy it.


00:18:51.047 --> 00:18:54.883
New intel suggests Cobalt
is already en route, leaving you. ..


00:18:54.967 --> 00:18:57.552
...4 hours 52 minutes...


00:18:57.637 --> 00:18:58.929
...to infiltrate.


00:18:59.013 --> 00:19:01.681
To save time,
we've chosen your team for you.


00:19:01.766 --> 00:19:03.141
Agents Carter and Dunn.


00:19:05.895 --> 00:19:10.065
As always, should you or any member
of your team be caught or killed,


00:19:10.149 --> 00:19:13.151
the Secretary will disavow
any knowledge of your actions.


00:19:13.236 --> 00:19:15.737
This message
will self-destruct in five seconds.


00:19:15.822 --> 00:19:17.072
Good luck, Ethan.


00:19:40.888 --> 00:19:42.222
What do you got?


00:19:46.894 --> 00:19:48.895
We're going into the Kremlin.


00:19:51.107 --> 00:19:56.820
I thought you said "The Kremlin."


00:19:59.282 --> 00:20:00.532
Okay.


00:20:37.987 --> 00:20:39.988
This is very exciting.


00:20:41.449 --> 00:20:42.949
Being out in the field.


00:20:43.284 --> 00:20:44.784
With you, you know.


00:20:45.161 --> 00:20:47.454
It's a bit of a dream for me.


00:20:49.665 --> 00:20:53.084
Love your disguise, by the way.
You look just like him.


00:20:53.628 --> 00:20:57.464
It's a shame we're not wearing masks.
You know, like, full masks.


00:20:58.466 --> 00:21:00.967
Everybody gets to
wear a mask but Benji.


00:21:02.053 --> 00:21:03.053
Sorry.


00:21:03.137 --> 00:21:04.930
I'm tense. I babble when I'm nervous.


00:21:05.014 --> 00:21:06.973
I'm doing it again. Shut up, Benji.


00:21:20.988 --> 00:21:22.572
Okay, seven security guards.


00:21:22.657 --> 00:21:25.283
X-ray machines. Cameras.
Metal detectors.


00:21:25.368 --> 00:21:27.535
Just what we expected. We can do this.


00:21:32.500 --> 00:21:35.835
Releasing in three, two, one.


00:21:42.843 --> 00:21:45.679
Game face, game face.
Kremlin game face.


00:21:49.392 --> 00:21:50.892
General...


00:21:51.894 --> 00:21:53.061
I am Major Egorov.


00:21:53.771 --> 00:21:55.063
Your documents.


00:22:01.821 --> 00:22:04.614
You should know your boss.


00:22:30.016 --> 00:22:31.433
I can't find you.


00:22:37.398 --> 00:22:38.690
Run it again...


00:22:38.774 --> 00:22:39.899
...Private.


00:22:39.984 --> 00:22:41.526
Egorov.


00:22:51.620 --> 00:22:54.539
Excuse me, General. I didn't recognize you.


00:22:55.916 --> 00:22:58.418
You're going to regret this, Egorov.


00:23:07.261 --> 00:23:09.304
I think that went quite well.


00:23:09.472 --> 00:23:10.472
Just shut it.


00:23:10.598 --> 00:23:11.598
Sorry.


00:24:36.016 --> 00:24:37.016
It's going to work.


00:24:38.352 --> 00:24:42.021
I'm sorry, by the way.
About you and Julia.


00:24:43.524 --> 00:24:45.358
You know, not working out.


00:24:45.693 --> 00:24:49.112
I wanted to say something
before you went away, but. ..


00:24:49.196 --> 00:24:50.572
I liked her, you know.


00:24:51.699 --> 00:24:53.366
He's off the phone now.


00:28:30.626 --> 00:28:31.959
It's empty.


00:28:33.128 --> 00:28:34.504
The nest is empty.


00:28:49.436 --> 00:28:50.728
Check in, Team Leader.


00:28:50.938 --> 00:28:51.938
Over.


00:28:52.106 --> 00:28:54.273
Repeat. Check in, Team Leader.


00:28:55.025 --> 00:28:56.776
Have you made it to the Archive Room?


00:28:57.069 --> 00:28:58.736
Captain! The Archive Room!


00:28:58.987 --> 00:28:59.987
Run!


00:29:02.366 --> 00:29:03.491
Someone is piggybacking our frequency.


00:29:04.827 --> 00:29:05.827
Team Leader,


00:29:05.911 --> 00:29:09.747
awaiting your go-sign.
Standing by to detonate.


00:29:09.873 --> 00:29:10.957
Abort.


00:29:14.628 --> 00:29:16.295
Rendezvous nine-two.


00:30:36.835 --> 00:30:37.960
Shut the gate!


00:30:39.838 --> 00:30:40.838
Quickly!


00:32:32.492 --> 00:32:34.160
Our media is no more
truthful than yours,


00:32:35.037 --> 00:32:36.495
American.


00:32:37.164 --> 00:32:40.833
But we both know
that the real cause of the explosion


00:32:41.168 --> 00:32:42.501
was you.


00:32:47.841 --> 00:32:49.967
Awaiting your go-sign, Team Leader.


00:32:50.052 --> 00:32:52.053
Standing by to detonate.


00:32:53.013 --> 00:32:54.513
The worst part for you,


00:32:55.307 --> 00:32:56.599
"Team Leader,"


00:32:57.434 --> 00:33:00.728
is I am the man assigned
to make you suffer for it.


00:33:01.188 --> 00:33:03.397
For what you did to my country.


00:33:06.234 --> 00:33:08.235
This is a hospital. ..


00:33:08.737 --> 00:33:09.737
Not a night club.


00:33:10.405 --> 00:33:11.739
Misha. ..help me here...


00:33:13.075 --> 00:33:14.075
Room twelve.


00:33:28.298 --> 00:33:32.009
The doctors say he's lucky to be alive.


00:33:35.430 --> 00:33:37.515
Only a mild concussion.


00:33:37.683 --> 00:33:39.600
I don't give a damn about his health.


00:33:42.270 --> 00:33:45.314
I have questions that need answering.


00:33:47.526 --> 00:33:48.776
Be careful!


00:33:50.737 --> 00:33:52.071
Prepare a transport.


00:33:57.661 --> 00:33:58.661
Check over there!


00:34:39.995 --> 00:34:41.662
Not a good idea.


00:34:43.123 --> 00:34:45.958
It seemed like one a minute ago.


00:35:39.596 --> 00:35:42.890
All agents! Hot target heading west!


00:36:02.202 --> 00:36:03.327
Consolidated Insurance.


00:36:03.411 --> 00:36:04.453
How may I help you?


00:36:04.538 --> 00:36:08.499
SAT 20. Agent 82-Delta-Echo
requesting immediate evac.


00:36:08.834 --> 00:36:11.126
Rendezvous Alpha 113.


00:36:11.211 --> 00:36:14.046
Confirmed. Alpha 113.


00:36:37.404 --> 00:36:40.364
Details surrounding
the intricate system of gas lines


00:36:40.448 --> 00:36:43.117
that run beneath the square
are still forthcoming,


00:36:43.201 --> 00:36:46.203
but the majority of
those lines date back to the Soviet era


00:36:46.288 --> 00:36:48.497
and have not been updated in at least. ..


00:36:48.915 --> 00:36:53.878
Anna... Anna. .. I've been thinking...


00:36:54.963 --> 00:36:55.963
It looks like we...


00:37:00.635 --> 00:37:02.720
We should leave town
for a couple of days.


00:37:02.804 --> 00:37:05.431
Alex, you, me. Vacations.


00:37:06.391 --> 00:37:07.766
- Now?
- Tonight.


00:37:07.893 --> 00:37:09.727
Why are you speaking in English?


00:37:10.520 --> 00:37:12.062
Just...


00:37:12.147 --> 00:37:13.898
Just the three of us.


00:37:13.982 --> 00:37:17.735
...may not have been an accident,
but a targeted attack.


00:37:19.112 --> 00:37:20.446
Preliminary numbers are just starting. ..


00:37:20.530 --> 00:37:21.864
Where will we go?


00:37:21.948 --> 00:37:24.241
...to come in regarding
those wounded in the blast.


00:37:24.326 --> 00:37:26.577
We can confirm that 11 tourists...


00:37:26.661 --> 00:37:27.745
Leonid?


00:37:27.829 --> 00:37:29.246
. ..their nationalities still unconfirmed,


00:37:29.331 --> 00:37:32.666
have been transported
to area hospitals for treatment.


00:37:33.084 --> 00:37:36.462
While Russian officials continue
to blame a gas-main break,


00:37:36.546 --> 00:37:40.925
experts are citing the shape of the blast
area and the size of the debris field


00:37:41.009 --> 00:37:43.761
as more consistent
with that of a set explosive,


00:37:43.845 --> 00:37:45.846
leading to speculation
that this may have been


00:37:45.931 --> 00:37:48.182
an undeclared act of aggression.


00:37:48.266 --> 00:37:50.434
Although the Defense Ministry
is maintaining


00:37:50.518 --> 00:37:51.852
that this is strictly an accident. ..


00:37:51.937 --> 00:37:54.647
Anna, pack a bag for Alex.


00:37:55.941 --> 00:37:57.316
We're leaving now.


00:37:58.735 --> 00:38:03.030
Anya!


00:38:15.126 --> 00:38:16.877
We have work to do.


00:38:46.741 --> 00:38:47.783
Mr. Secretary.


00:38:52.122 --> 00:38:53.455
I wasn't aware you were in Russia.


00:38:53.540 --> 00:38:57.126
I'm not.
Not since a bomb blew up the Kremlin.


00:39:01.589 --> 00:39:04.299
Yesterday I flew in
to accept the Order of Friendship


00:39:04.426 --> 00:39:05.926
from the Russian Prime Minister.


00:39:06.136 --> 00:39:08.679
Now I'm headed back to Washington


00:39:08.763 --> 00:39:11.432
to hand the President my resignation.


00:39:14.436 --> 00:39:16.812
My Chief Analyst, William Brandt.


00:39:18.440 --> 00:39:19.690
Do you have a pen?


00:39:19.774 --> 00:39:20.774
- Pardon me?
- A pen.


00:39:22.277 --> 00:39:23.402
Yeah.


00:39:25.572 --> 00:39:27.239
Ethan, what happened in the Kremlin?


00:39:28.658 --> 00:39:29.658
Chief Analyst, you say?


00:39:29.743 --> 00:39:31.535
If you're implying that
I made a bad call...


00:39:31.619 --> 00:39:32.828
European male.


00:39:32.912 --> 00:39:36.206
Fifties. About six-foot,
180 pounds. Blue eyes.


00:39:36.291 --> 00:39:37.624
Who is he?


00:39:39.419 --> 00:39:42.296
A crude drawing,
but by your description,


00:39:42.380 --> 00:39:43.756
that could be Kurt Hendricks.


00:39:43.840 --> 00:39:47.426
190 IQ. Served in
Swedish Special Forces.


00:39:47.510 --> 00:39:50.429
Professor of physics,
Stockholm University.


00:39:50.513 --> 00:39:52.222
Specialist in nuclear endgame theory.


00:39:52.307 --> 00:39:53.974
Asked to resign...


00:39:55.602 --> 00:39:57.269
Well, because he's crazy.


00:39:58.271 --> 00:39:59.271
Cobalt.


00:40:02.484 --> 00:40:04.568
You have to alert the Kremlin
that one of their strategists


00:40:04.652 --> 00:40:06.070
has a nuclear launch device


00:40:06.488 --> 00:40:09.281
and one of his operatives
has the codes to activate it.


00:40:09.365 --> 00:40:10.616
And what makes you say that?


00:40:11.868 --> 00:40:12.868
I saw him


00:40:13.787 --> 00:40:16.288
leaving the executive armory,
bag in hand.


00:40:16.372 --> 00:40:18.665
He set off that explosion
to cover his tracks.


00:40:18.750 --> 00:40:20.876
It could be weeks
before the Russians know it's missing.


00:40:20.960 --> 00:40:22.086
Unless we tell them.


00:40:22.170 --> 00:40:23.712
They won't listen to us.


00:40:23.797 --> 00:40:27.758
As far as the Russians are concerned,
we just bombed the Kremlin.


00:40:28.384 --> 00:40:30.803
The tension between
the United States and Russia


00:40:30.887 --> 00:40:33.889
hasn't been this high
since the Cuban Missile Crisis.


00:40:34.265 --> 00:40:38.352
And the blame, right or wrong,
points to IMF.


00:40:43.066 --> 00:40:46.735
The President has initiated
Ghost Protocol.


00:40:47.445 --> 00:40:50.531
The entire IMF has been disavowed.


00:40:53.535 --> 00:40:55.494
So what happens now?


00:40:55.578 --> 00:40:58.914
Now, I've been ordered
to take you back to Washington,


00:40:58.998 --> 00:41:02.042
where the DOD will label you
as a rogue extremist


00:41:02.210 --> 00:41:04.753
and hang the Kremlin bombing
on you and your team.


00:41:05.755 --> 00:41:07.131
Unless,


00:41:07.882 --> 00:41:09.466
you were to escape


00:41:09.551 --> 00:41:12.761
somewhere between here
and the airport,


00:41:12.846 --> 00:41:16.473
having assaulted Mr. Brandt and me.


00:41:16.558 --> 00:41:17.558
Sir?


00:41:18.560 --> 00:41:19.810
You would then


00:41:19.894 --> 00:41:21.854
illegally scrounge
whatever material you could


00:41:21.938 --> 00:41:24.481
from a backup supply cache
that I've overlooked.


00:41:24.566 --> 00:41:27.901
The same cache where
your team are waiting for further orders.


00:41:27.986 --> 00:41:28.986
Sir, you may want to. ..


00:41:29.070 --> 00:41:33.866
You will then disappear, and this
conversation never having taken place,


00:41:33.950 --> 00:41:36.618
your intentions would be unclear.


00:41:36.703 --> 00:41:40.497
But if any one of your team
is caught or killed,


00:41:40.582 --> 00:41:42.708
they will be branded terrorists,


00:41:42.792 --> 00:41:46.295
out to incite global nuclear war.


00:41:53.428 --> 00:41:54.511
Your mission,


00:41:55.722 --> 00:41:57.848
should you choose to accept it.


00:42:02.437 --> 00:42:04.688
Ethan, you were my best man.


00:42:05.940 --> 00:42:07.733
And I'm sorry it's come to this,


00:42:07.817 --> 00:42:10.319
after all the sacrifices you made.


00:42:12.614 --> 00:42:14.781
If we don't meet again,
I just want you to know,


00:42:16.034 --> 00:42:17.451
I've always considered you a friend.


00:42:19.787 --> 00:42:21.663
Stay down! Drive, drive, drive!


00:42:48.358 --> 00:42:49.358
You okay?


00:42:49.484 --> 00:42:50.484
Yeah.


00:42:51.027 --> 00:42:53.737
Take a deep breath. Stay with me.


00:42:53.821 --> 00:42:55.113
- Ready?
- Yeah.


00:43:19.681 --> 00:43:21.014
What do we do?


00:43:22.517 --> 00:43:23.600
Wait here.


00:43:25.853 --> 00:43:27.688
Where else am I going to go?


00:43:42.829 --> 00:43:44.579
Hey! Hey, hey, hey!


00:43:58.386 --> 00:44:00.846
Hold your fire! Hold your fire!


00:44:01.556 --> 00:44:04.933
Hold your fire!


00:44:05.184 --> 00:44:06.393
Weapons down!


00:44:08.062 --> 00:44:09.771
What are you firing at?


00:44:31.210 --> 00:44:34.379
Two prisoners escaped from Rankow Prison today.


00:44:42.263 --> 00:44:43.263
And this one?...


00:44:44.307 --> 00:44:45.849
What do we know about him?


00:44:49.687 --> 00:44:51.146
Why would that work?


00:44:52.774 --> 00:44:53.982
Why would what work?


00:44:54.067 --> 00:44:56.193
The flare on the body,
why would that work?


00:44:56.277 --> 00:44:57.444
It did work.


00:44:57.528 --> 00:44:59.363
- Yeah, I know, but...
- Hey!


00:44:59.447 --> 00:45:03.700
But why? I mean, how did you know
that would draw their fire?


00:45:03.785 --> 00:45:05.952
I didn't. I played a hunch.


00:45:07.622 --> 00:45:10.957
Okay. All right,
so what was your scenario?


00:45:11.042 --> 00:45:13.794
Right, you. ..
There's a guy being shot at in the water.


00:45:13.878 --> 00:45:17.005
All of a sudden, decides to light up
a flare and swim around?


00:45:18.132 --> 00:45:20.759
I mean, what did you assume
they'd be thinking?


00:45:20.843 --> 00:45:22.552
- Thinking?
- Yeah.


00:45:22.637 --> 00:45:25.514
I didn't assume they were thinking.


00:45:25.598 --> 00:45:27.599
I assumed they were shooting
at anything that moved.


00:45:27.683 --> 00:45:30.060
I just gave them a target. Look, these. ..


00:45:30.144 --> 00:45:32.938
These guys aren't
Rhodes Scholars, you know?


00:45:37.026 --> 00:45:38.652
It's really happening, isn't it?


00:45:39.487 --> 00:45:40.529
Yeah.


00:45:41.656 --> 00:45:43.115
Okay, you know what that sound is?


00:45:43.199 --> 00:45:45.033
That's our ride out of here!


00:45:45.118 --> 00:45:48.328
All right, it's a green car. Number 47.


00:45:51.541 --> 00:45:53.083
I see green!


00:45:53.167 --> 00:45:54.751
Okay, let's do it.


00:45:54.836 --> 00:45:56.336
Go, go, go, go.


00:45:58.005 --> 00:46:00.132
All right, 47.


00:46:00.216 --> 00:46:01.466
I don't see it.


00:46:01.551 --> 00:46:03.009
47.


00:46:03.094 --> 00:46:04.428
Oh, shit!


00:46:10.852 --> 00:46:12.936
This is it. The manifest.


00:46:13.020 --> 00:46:14.604
Enter your code.


00:46:14.689 --> 00:46:15.689
Pole!


00:46:18.693 --> 00:46:19.860
Jeez...


00:46:21.404 --> 00:46:22.904
Press enter.


00:46:25.241 --> 00:46:26.616
Retinal scanner!


00:46:30.204 --> 00:46:32.456
Retinal scan required.


00:46:32.540 --> 00:46:33.874
Watch out!


00:46:34.667 --> 00:46:36.668
Retinal scan required.


00:46:36.752 --> 00:46:38.378
Agent confirmed.


00:46:51.934 --> 00:46:54.686
Ethan? Jeez, I thought you were dead!


00:46:54.770 --> 00:46:56.521
- We are.
- Who's this?


00:46:56.606 --> 00:46:59.983
Agents Dunn and Carter.
William Brandt, Chief Analyst.


00:47:00.067 --> 00:47:01.401
Analyst?


00:47:06.240 --> 00:47:07.908
Agent confirmed.


00:47:15.416 --> 00:47:18.126
How will the world finally end?


00:47:19.295 --> 00:47:22.255
It is my job to predict the unthinkable.


00:47:23.799 --> 00:47:26.343
To treat the death of billions as a game.


00:47:27.970 --> 00:47:31.306
After 20 years of this, I was numb.


00:47:32.141 --> 00:47:35.143
Until a new question crossed my mind.


00:47:36.103 --> 00:47:38.939
What happens after
the end of the world?


00:47:39.106 --> 00:47:41.233
Are you sure your line is secure?


00:47:41.317 --> 00:47:43.068
Every two or three million years...


00:47:43.152 --> 00:47:46.238
Are you certain your line is secure?


00:47:46.322 --> 00:47:50.408
. ..some natural catastrophe
devastates all life on Earth.


00:47:50.493 --> 00:47:52.160
But life goes on.


00:47:52.495 --> 00:47:56.081
And what little remains
is made stronger.


00:47:56.165 --> 00:48:00.210
Put simply,
world destruction is an unpleasant,


00:48:00.294 --> 00:48:02.671
but necessary part of evolution.


00:48:05.299 --> 00:48:07.384
What happens then, I wondered,


00:48:07.718 --> 00:48:10.095
when mankind faces
the next end of the world?


00:48:10.179 --> 00:48:13.223
I don't care what you have to do
to get him to Dubai.


00:48:13.307 --> 00:48:15.767
I'll make it worth his while. Just do it.


00:48:15.851 --> 00:48:18.395
I looked to Hiroshima, Nagasaki...


00:48:18.479 --> 00:48:19.604
I'll be waiting for your call.


00:48:19.689 --> 00:48:22.232
. ..thriving cities rebuilt from the ashes,


00:48:22.316 --> 00:48:24.651
monuments to the unimaginable,


00:48:24.735 --> 00:48:26.611
dedicated to the concept of peace.


00:48:27.321 --> 00:48:31.825
It occurred to me here
that nuclear war might have a place


00:48:31.909 --> 00:48:33.410
in the natural order.


00:48:33.494 --> 00:48:35.537
But only if it could be controlled.


00:48:35.997 --> 00:48:40.208
Only if it touched
every living soul equally.


00:48:41.711 --> 00:48:44.754
IMF now believes this man,
Kurt Hendricks,


00:48:44.839 --> 00:48:47.799
is the nuclear extremist,
code name Cobalt.


00:48:47.883 --> 00:48:49.801
Today he was seen leaving the Kremlin,


00:48:49.885 --> 00:48:52.554
with what is likely
a nuclear launch device.


00:48:54.932 --> 00:48:58.018
Two days ago, Sabine Moreau killed
one of our agents in Budapest


00:48:58.102 --> 00:49:00.770
and relieved him
of Russian nuclear launch codes.


00:49:00.855 --> 00:49:05.358
Intel indicates she will check into
the Burj Hotel in Dubai in 36 hours.


00:49:06.611 --> 00:49:08.778
Marius Wistrom
is a known operative of Cobalt.


00:49:09.030 --> 00:49:11.323
Wistrom is currently en route to Dubai.


00:49:11.407 --> 00:49:15.118
For the launch device to work,
Cobalt needs the activation codes.


00:49:15.202 --> 00:49:18.038
He's sending Wistrom
to buy them from Moreau.


00:49:19.040 --> 00:49:20.540
The Secretary


00:49:22.084 --> 00:49:23.293
is dead.


00:49:28.633 --> 00:49:31.468
The President
has invoked Ghost Protocol.


00:49:32.178 --> 00:49:33.762
We're shut down.


00:49:33.888 --> 00:49:37.849
No satellite, safe house,
support, or extraction.


00:49:37.933 --> 00:49:41.144
The four of us
and the contents of this car


00:49:41.228 --> 00:49:43.855
are all that remain of the IMF.


00:49:43.939 --> 00:49:48.318
And as of this moment, any action
is unsanctioned. So if you want out,


00:49:48.402 --> 00:49:49.736
speak now.


00:50:06.253 --> 00:50:07.504
Our mission is Hendricks.


00:50:07.880 --> 00:50:09.714
We're all that stands
between him and his goal.


00:50:09.799 --> 00:50:11.049
Nothing can be left to chance.


00:50:11.133 --> 00:50:13.176
Everyone connected with this man


00:50:13.260 --> 00:50:16.513
is considered an asset with valuable
information about our target.


00:50:16.597 --> 00:50:18.014
No one can know we're still on line.


00:50:18.099 --> 00:50:20.392
We lose Hendricks now,
we lose him forever.


00:50:20.476 --> 00:50:22.060
So, what's the play?


00:50:22.144 --> 00:50:24.771
Wistrom will take delivery from Moreau
in 36 hours.


00:50:24.855 --> 00:50:27.023
Now we cannot let
the launch codes leave the hotel,


00:50:27.108 --> 00:50:29.984
but we need Wistrom
to lead us to Hendricks.


00:50:30.069 --> 00:50:32.195
He'll only do that if he has the codes.


00:50:32.279 --> 00:50:33.697
Or if he thinks he has them.


00:50:33.781 --> 00:50:35.990
Our objective is to intercept the sale,


00:50:36.075 --> 00:50:38.368
replace the authentic
codes with counterfeits


00:50:38.452 --> 00:50:40.203
and follow Wistrom to Hendricks.


00:50:40.287 --> 00:50:41.705
Well, that's simple enough.


00:50:41.789 --> 00:50:43.957
We snatch the codes,
we gin up some fakes.


00:50:44.041 --> 00:50:48.712
Jane, you double Moreau, and sell the
codes to Wistrom and Bob's your uncle.


00:50:48.796 --> 00:50:52.215
And how do you propose
we just snatch the codes from Moreau?


00:50:52.299 --> 00:50:53.299
We take her out.


00:50:55.469 --> 00:50:58.221
Yeah, we take her out.
But, you know, discreetly.


00:50:58.305 --> 00:50:59.472
Discreetly?


00:51:00.099 --> 00:51:01.224
Yeah.


00:51:02.268 --> 00:51:05.645
Right, she's an asset. Right. I get it.
Sorry. Nothing left to chance.


00:51:05.730 --> 00:51:08.231
He said. .. I'm spitballing.
It's not all gonna be gold.


00:51:08.315 --> 00:51:09.941
- We don't touch Wistrom.
- All right.


00:51:10.025 --> 00:51:11.025
Or Moreau.


00:51:13.362 --> 00:51:16.448
She'll answer for Hanaway,
but it has to be when I say.


00:51:16.532 --> 00:51:18.241
After we hit Hendricks.


00:51:24.290 --> 00:51:25.498
Only pack what we need.


00:51:25.583 --> 00:51:28.168
Yeah, absolutely. Only pack what we...
You never know.


00:51:56.030 --> 00:51:58.490
So even if we can double
Wistrom and Moreau,


00:51:59.241 --> 00:52:01.367
how do we keep them in separate rooms


00:52:01.452 --> 00:52:04.120
while having them think that
they're in the same room?


00:52:04.205 --> 00:52:06.206
We give the hotel a facelift.


00:52:06.457 --> 00:52:09.167
Wistrom will think
he's arriving at Moreau's suite,


00:52:09.251 --> 00:52:11.503
but, really, he'll be
walking into our decoy room.


00:52:11.629 --> 00:52:13.129
Where I'll double Moreau.


00:52:13.380 --> 00:52:14.756
Downstairs, Benji will double Wistrom.


00:52:15.216 --> 00:52:16.216
Masks!


00:52:16.300 --> 00:52:17.759
And meet with the real Moreau.


00:52:17.968 --> 00:52:19.344
And...


00:52:20.054 --> 00:52:21.221
What am I doing?


00:52:21.972 --> 00:52:24.474
You? You're the helper!


00:52:27.394 --> 00:52:28.770
Helper. That's great.


00:52:29.313 --> 00:52:33.316
Okay, so to the extent I understand
what you're talking about here. ..


00:52:34.568 --> 00:52:36.986
The Burj Khalifa,
it's the tallest building in the world,


00:52:37.071 --> 00:52:39.364
and you want to alter its infrastructure


00:52:39.448 --> 00:52:42.242
with the hopes of convincing
two people that they've


00:52:42.326 --> 00:52:45.662
had a meeting,
which actually really never happened.


00:52:46.413 --> 00:52:47.413
Right?


00:52:56.090 --> 00:52:57.090
Camels.


00:53:44.638 --> 00:53:46.806
ETA on dry cleaning.


00:53:46.891 --> 00:53:48.391
On my way up.


00:53:51.937 --> 00:53:53.771
Okay, 34 minutes to door knock.


00:53:57.610 --> 00:53:59.319
Wow. ..


00:54:00.654 --> 00:54:04.782
Okay, this is a slight wrinkle,
but nothing to worry about.


00:54:04.867 --> 00:54:08.202
We're just going to have to go into
the server room from the outside.


00:54:09.413 --> 00:54:10.413
What?


00:54:10.956 --> 00:54:14.208
Well, the firewalls on this building's
server are military grade.


00:54:14.293 --> 00:54:16.127
I mean, this would be a cinch


00:54:16.211 --> 00:54:17.629
if I could call Youssef
back at headquarters,


00:54:17.713 --> 00:54:19.714
but Youssef doesn't exist anymore,
and neither do we.


00:54:19.798 --> 00:54:21.215
I could hack it,
but it would take too long.


00:54:21.300 --> 00:54:22.425
Then hardwire in.


00:54:22.509 --> 00:54:24.052
And there's four layers
of next-gen security


00:54:24.136 --> 00:54:25.428
between us and the server room.


00:54:25.512 --> 00:54:27.305
There's no way
we can get to it from inside.


00:54:28.015 --> 00:54:30.558
If we can't get to the server,
we don't control the elevators,


00:54:30.643 --> 00:54:32.518
we don't control the security cameras.


00:54:32.603 --> 00:54:34.687
This operation is over
before it even begins.


00:54:34.772 --> 00:54:36.773
I'm telling you,
we can get to it from outside.


00:54:36.857 --> 00:54:37.857
"We"?


00:54:39.109 --> 00:54:40.360
I'm. .. I'm on the computer.


00:54:42.446 --> 00:54:44.197
I'm just...


00:54:44.281 --> 00:54:45.615
The helper.


00:54:48.953 --> 00:54:50.203
What floor is it on?


00:54:50.287 --> 00:54:51.871
130.


00:54:52.623 --> 00:54:54.290
130?


00:54:58.545 --> 00:54:59.671
- Vent ducts.
- Pressure sensitive.


00:54:59.755 --> 00:55:00.755
Not enough time.


00:55:00.839 --> 00:55:02.298
- Elevator shaft.
- Infrared sensors.


00:55:02.383 --> 00:55:03.383
Not enough time.


00:55:06.971 --> 00:55:08.721
How am I supposed to do this?


00:55:14.853 --> 00:55:16.354
God damn it!


00:55:19.858 --> 00:55:21.192
Oh, that's high.


00:55:26.740 --> 00:55:30.743
Okay, now remember, it's a rolling off
motion that disengages the bond.


00:55:30.828 --> 00:55:32.996
When the meter is blue,
that's full adhesion.


00:55:33.080 --> 00:55:35.248
Easy way to remember, blue is glue.


00:55:35.332 --> 00:55:36.791
- And when it's red?
- Dead.


00:55:36.875 --> 00:55:39.752
Here's your cutter, okay?
And your server interface.


00:55:39.837 --> 00:55:42.672
Both going back here. One, two.


00:55:43.007 --> 00:55:46.843
Okay, Ethan, the hotel server is
eleven stories up and seven units over.


00:55:46.927 --> 00:55:48.928
Okay? Comm check.


00:55:49.680 --> 00:55:51.180
Yeah. Copy.


00:55:52.766 --> 00:55:53.933
So. ..


00:55:57.938 --> 00:56:00.440
It's 26 minutes to door knock.


00:56:02.443 --> 00:56:03.651
Yeah.


00:56:58.290 --> 00:57:00.458
25 minutes to door knock.


00:57:15.474 --> 00:57:16.849
What the hell is that?


00:57:32.199 --> 00:57:34.492
Yeah, what the hell is that?


00:57:35.994 --> 00:57:37.703
It's a sandstorm.


00:57:39.832 --> 00:57:40.915
It's a long way off, Ethan.


00:57:40.999 --> 00:57:42.375
Shouldn't be a problem.


00:57:45.337 --> 00:57:47.880
24 minutes to door knock.


00:57:50.843 --> 00:57:51.968
Where's Ethan?


00:57:55.013 --> 00:57:56.389
You've got to be kidding me.


00:58:46.231 --> 00:58:49.400
23 minutes to door knock.


00:59:08.045 --> 00:59:09.378
I'm at server level.


00:59:32.152 --> 00:59:33.486
22 minutes to door knock.


00:59:34.738 --> 00:59:37.240
The countdown is not helping.


00:59:39.243 --> 00:59:40.243
I'm just saying.


01:00:10.607 --> 01:00:11.607
I'm in.


01:00:11.692 --> 01:00:13.109
That's great, Ethan.
You're halfway home.


01:00:20.951 --> 01:00:22.201
Located server.


01:00:29.293 --> 01:00:30.835
Please tell me we're online.


01:00:30.919 --> 01:00:32.211
All right, we're live.


01:00:32.504 --> 01:00:36.549
Okay, I now have control of
the elevators and the security cameras.


01:00:36.633 --> 01:00:37.633
Time to redecorate.


01:00:37.718 --> 01:00:40.636
Okay, you drive.
And look out for Wistrom and Moreau.


01:00:55.527 --> 01:00:57.737
Moreau is at the elevators
ahead of schedule.


01:00:58.739 --> 01:00:59.905
Go.


01:01:05.579 --> 01:01:07.204
We can't open this door, can we?


01:01:07.289 --> 01:01:08.581
The door? No.


01:01:08.665 --> 01:01:10.499
Ethan, you gotta get down here now.


01:01:11.877 --> 01:01:13.377
Ethan!


01:01:13.837 --> 01:01:16.088
Is there a problem? Ethan?


01:01:23.388 --> 01:01:24.388
We're not gonna make it.


01:01:24.473 --> 01:01:25.473
We have to make it.


01:01:26.725 --> 01:01:27.725
Where's Ethan?


01:01:50.457 --> 01:01:52.083
Your line's not long enough!


01:01:52.626 --> 01:01:53.918
No shit!


01:02:40.924 --> 01:02:42.591
That was not easy,


01:02:42.676 --> 01:02:44.343
but I did it.


01:02:46.763 --> 01:02:47.972
What'd I miss?


01:02:55.230 --> 01:02:58.732
The lens might be a little uncomfortable.


01:02:58.817 --> 01:03:01.652
It captures images and transmits them
to the printer in the briefcase.


01:03:02.779 --> 01:03:04.697
All right?


01:03:04.781 --> 01:03:07.283
I can't see out of one eye, but I'm fine.


01:03:07.367 --> 01:03:08.993
Blink twice to activate the shutter.


01:03:10.287 --> 01:03:11.871
Notice the numbers are in order?


01:03:15.375 --> 01:03:16.500
A perfect copy.


01:03:18.795 --> 01:03:20.463
But the numbers are scrambled.


01:03:22.132 --> 01:03:23.132
Masks?


01:03:23.216 --> 01:03:25.217
60 seconds.
You sure I shouldn't wear a mask?


01:03:25.302 --> 01:03:27.470
You know,
'cause I'm not exactly Omar Sharif.


01:03:27.554 --> 01:03:29.722
I'll play it French.
This is your tracking device.


01:03:29.806 --> 01:03:31.474
- This is what you're tracking.
- The paper clip?


01:03:31.558 --> 01:03:32.558
No, it's the paper.


01:03:32.642 --> 01:03:35.186
It's in the briefcase. It's coated with
isotopes which give off a unique...


01:03:35.270 --> 01:03:36.770
It just means
that you can track the documents


01:03:36.855 --> 01:03:37.980
even if they switch briefcases.


01:03:38.064 --> 01:03:39.023
Range?


01:03:39.107 --> 01:03:40.149
Not that good. It's, like, half a mile.


01:03:40.233 --> 01:03:42.401
Safest thing to do would be not let
Wistrom out of your sight.


01:03:42.486 --> 01:03:43.903
Is that Wistrom?


01:03:48.325 --> 01:03:49.325
Who's that with him?


01:03:49.409 --> 01:03:51.994
I don't know. We don't have an uplink,
so there's no facial recognition.


01:03:52.078 --> 01:03:53.496
Who's that with him?


01:03:54.831 --> 01:03:57.500
That's Leonid Lisenker.
Polish-born cryptographer.


01:03:57.584 --> 01:04:00.002
He redesigned Russia's nuclear
security after the Cold War.


01:04:00.670 --> 01:04:02.671
He's here to authenticate
the launch codes.


01:04:02.756 --> 01:04:04.840
- Yes, he is. We are blown.
- No, we're not blown.


01:04:04.925 --> 01:04:07.134
Well, we will be as soon as he sees
the counterfeit launch codes.


01:04:07.219 --> 01:04:08.219
We're not blown.


01:04:09.012 --> 01:04:10.054
He's in the elevator.


01:04:10.138 --> 01:04:11.347
Delay them.


01:04:20.690 --> 01:04:22.483
Benji, how long would it take you
to reprogram the case?


01:04:22.567 --> 01:04:24.777
A couple of seconds. What for, though?


01:04:24.861 --> 01:04:27.029
To make an exact copy
of the launch codes.


01:04:27.113 --> 01:04:28.697
- What?
- You can't do that.


01:04:28.782 --> 01:04:30.282
- Wistrom's on 22!
- Slow him down.


01:04:30.367 --> 01:04:31.367
I'll do what I can.


01:04:34.204 --> 01:04:35.788
Wait, wait. Ethan, hang on now!


01:04:35.872 --> 01:04:37.206
Hang on. Just a second.


01:04:37.290 --> 01:04:40.793
You're talking about handing over active
nuclear launch codes to Wistrom?


01:04:40.877 --> 01:04:41.961
Yes. Reprogram the case.


01:04:42.045 --> 01:04:43.045
Listen... Stop!


01:04:43.129 --> 01:04:44.129
Just listen to what you're saying.


01:04:44.214 --> 01:04:46.006
You're fixating.
You're not thinking clearly.


01:04:46.091 --> 01:04:49.134
It's not gonna happen. I won't let it!


01:04:49.219 --> 01:04:50.553
33 and climbing!


01:04:50.637 --> 01:04:51.804
Brandt, use your head now.


01:04:51.888 --> 01:04:53.597
The mission is not the codes,
the mission is Hendricks.


01:04:53.682 --> 01:04:56.100
Then just let it play out.
Give him bad codes. Neutralize him.


01:04:56.184 --> 01:04:57.226
You know that won't do it.


01:04:57.310 --> 01:04:59.895
Failure to a terrorist
is just a rehearsal for success.


01:04:59.980 --> 01:05:01.313
41!


01:05:01.398 --> 01:05:03.649
We lose Hendricks today,
he shows up somewhere else tomorrow.


01:05:03.733 --> 01:05:04.817
He finds another way.


01:05:04.901 --> 01:05:06.402
With no IMF to stop him.


01:05:06.486 --> 01:05:08.654
No. It's now or never.
Now, Brandt, give me the case.


01:05:08.738 --> 01:05:10.906
Nothing can be left to chance.
You said that.


01:05:10.991 --> 01:05:11.991
You're the analyst.


01:05:12.075 --> 01:05:14.159
Now, tell me there's not another way
for Hendricks to get those codes.


01:05:14.244 --> 01:05:15.244
50!


01:05:15.328 --> 01:05:17.913
You tell me that this is his only avenue,
right here, right now, today.


01:05:17.998 --> 01:05:20.416
You tell me that, I'll walk away.


01:05:28.091 --> 01:05:29.758
- We go without.
- Without masks?


01:05:29.843 --> 01:05:31.135
- Jane needs to go.
- Ethan!


01:05:31.219 --> 01:05:32.219
We have no choice.


01:05:32.304 --> 01:05:33.929
Ethan, you'd be walking in
on Moreau unarmed.


01:05:34.014 --> 01:05:35.264
Face-first. Literally.


01:05:35.348 --> 01:05:36.348
How do we know they've met?


01:05:36.600 --> 01:05:38.434
- How do we know they haven't?
- Doesn't matter!


01:05:39.769 --> 01:05:41.103
Damn it.


01:05:41.354 --> 01:05:42.688
We have no choice.


01:06:34.157 --> 01:06:35.491
Goggles.


01:06:37.827 --> 01:06:39.411
What if they have met?


01:06:41.915 --> 01:06:43.832
Come in.


01:07:18.702 --> 01:07:23.372
Which one of you is Wistrom?


01:07:26.209 --> 01:07:27.543
I am.


01:07:29.045 --> 01:07:30.879
I admire your work.


01:07:46.312 --> 01:07:47.479
Sit.


01:07:56.406 --> 01:07:57.990
Where are my codes?


01:07:59.492 --> 01:08:00.993
Where are my diamonds?


01:08:02.162 --> 01:08:03.412
Close by.


01:08:04.330 --> 01:08:05.664
You have my payment?


01:08:05.915 --> 01:08:07.624
When I see the codes.


01:08:08.752 --> 01:08:10.461
Not to worry. Come in!


01:08:11.254 --> 01:08:12.921
I thought we could have tea.


01:08:20.263 --> 01:08:22.598
No diamonds, no codes.


01:08:23.099 --> 01:08:25.434
No codes, no diamonds.


01:08:29.397 --> 01:08:30.397
Kill this one.


01:08:30.482 --> 01:08:32.441
We didn't come alone.


01:08:32.776 --> 01:08:34.443
That hallway out there is a kill-box.


01:08:34.611 --> 01:08:35.944
You know who we work for.


01:08:36.029 --> 01:08:38.530
We come back with the codes,
or we don't come back.


01:08:40.450 --> 01:08:41.784
How good is your backup?


01:08:42.035 --> 01:08:43.452
The best.


01:08:46.873 --> 01:08:49.166
I've killed the best.


01:08:50.126 --> 01:08:51.794
Do you care for some sugar?


01:08:56.132 --> 01:08:57.800
Enough. Let's get this done.


01:08:58.134 --> 01:09:00.552
You want payment, I want guarantees.


01:09:01.137 --> 01:09:02.471
When he's authenticated the codes,


01:09:02.555 --> 01:09:05.057
I'll make the call
and you get your diamonds.


01:09:05.141 --> 01:09:06.809
That or


01:09:07.352 --> 01:09:09.353
we all go home in buckets.


01:09:10.313 --> 01:09:12.815
Nobody leaves this hotel alive.


01:09:16.528 --> 01:09:17.528
Get the papers.


01:09:32.335 --> 01:09:33.669
Is there a problem?


01:09:34.337 --> 01:09:35.671
It's locked.


01:09:39.676 --> 01:09:43.512
Forgive me. There must be a key.


01:09:44.681 --> 01:09:46.348
One moment, huh?


01:10:44.157 --> 01:10:48.201
My mistake.
It is a combination, not a key.


01:10:48.745 --> 01:10:50.412
You tell me the numbers.


01:10:56.377 --> 01:10:57.377
They're good.


01:10:57.670 --> 01:11:04.259
Zero.


01:11:21.444 --> 01:11:22.694
Come on, come on, come on.


01:12:06.155 --> 01:12:08.407
It was a pleasure doing business with...


01:12:08.491 --> 01:12:10.659
Wistrom has the launch codes.
He's on the move.


01:12:11.160 --> 01:12:14.663
Hey, I did as you asked. I did.
Now let my family go!


01:12:14.914 --> 01:12:16.331
Release Leonid's family.


01:12:16.416 --> 01:12:17.708
Thank God.


01:12:17.792 --> 01:12:19.251
You can thank him in person.


01:12:35.018 --> 01:12:37.436
It was a pleasure
doing business with you.


01:12:44.360 --> 01:12:45.360
Kill him!


01:12:54.037 --> 01:12:55.203
Moreau's on the move!


01:12:56.205 --> 01:12:57.539
I've got her.


01:12:58.875 --> 01:12:59.875
Jane?


01:12:59.959 --> 01:13:00.959
She's an asset!


01:13:01.169 --> 01:13:02.544
I need her


01:13:02.628 --> 01:13:03.628
alive!


01:13:05.006 --> 01:13:07.841
Acknowledge!


01:13:19.228 --> 01:13:22.731
Ethan, Wistrom is in the elevator.
I can't see Leonid, though.


01:13:24.609 --> 01:13:27.736
Benji, slow him down.
Get me an elevator.


01:13:40.083 --> 01:13:41.333
Find Leonid.


01:13:54.430 --> 01:13:57.140
Benji, I've got a lock on Wistrom.
But I can't tell.


01:13:57.225 --> 01:13:58.892
Is he still in the elevator?


01:14:00.353 --> 01:14:01.353
Benji?


01:14:05.358 --> 01:14:06.358
Ethan. Over?


01:14:06.442 --> 01:14:07.484
Benji.


01:14:07.568 --> 01:14:08.610
Benji, I lost. ..


01:14:08.694 --> 01:14:10.278
Ethan, can you hear me?


01:14:10.363 --> 01:14:11.863
Ethan, can you hear me? Over.


01:14:13.032 --> 01:14:14.199
Jesus!


01:14:20.373 --> 01:14:21.581
Sit down!


01:14:23.543 --> 01:14:25.210
- Watch her.
- Why me?


01:14:25.294 --> 01:14:26.795
Because if I do, I'll kill her.


01:14:56.576 --> 01:14:58.910
Hold it, Team Leader.


01:14:59.829 --> 01:15:02.330
Did you really think
I wouldn't catch up with you?


01:15:02.415 --> 01:15:04.416
You and I are not enemies.
It was a set-up...


01:15:04.500 --> 01:15:07.294
We'll find out your lies soon enough.


01:15:07.712 --> 01:15:08.920
Move it!


01:15:09.964 --> 01:15:11.548
I'm sorry about this.


01:15:34.322 --> 01:15:35.822
Leonid. Benji?


01:15:36.282 --> 01:15:37.324
Go for Benji.


01:15:37.408 --> 01:15:39.284
I've got Leonid by the elevators.
He's been shot.


01:15:39.368 --> 01:15:40.368
What?


01:15:51.214 --> 01:15:53.965
Hey, hey. Stay with me. Stay with me.


01:16:13.027 --> 01:16:14.611
No, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no, no.


01:16:20.952 --> 01:16:22.577
Jane! No!


01:19:23.926 --> 01:19:25.552
Come on. Come on.


01:22:19.184 --> 01:22:20.685
Now, what happened
with Moreau, Jane?


01:22:20.769 --> 01:22:21.811
She couldn't help us with Hendricks.


01:22:21.895 --> 01:22:23.438
So let's throw her off the building!


01:22:23.522 --> 01:22:24.522
I didn't throw her.


01:22:24.607 --> 01:22:25.607
Let's throw her off the building!


01:22:25.691 --> 01:22:28.151
She was not the mission, Jane!


01:22:28.235 --> 01:22:33.197
The mission was to track the file
back to Hendricks, who is in the wind


01:22:33.282 --> 01:22:35.450
with nuclear launch codes!


01:22:35.534 --> 01:22:38.286
Maybe you didn't notice the gun
she had pointed at me.


01:22:38.370 --> 01:22:40.622
Yeah, like you didn't notice
the open window,


01:22:40.706 --> 01:22:42.540
or that we're about a mile up in the air!


01:22:42.625 --> 01:22:44.292
It was an instinctive move.


01:22:44.376 --> 01:22:45.376
It doesn't matter!


01:22:45.461 --> 01:22:47.295
We're talking about a nuclear war.


01:22:47.379 --> 01:22:49.839
The asset is more important than you.


01:22:49.923 --> 01:22:52.300
Where do you get off telling me
how well I executed?


01:22:52.384 --> 01:22:53.593
We inherited you.


01:22:54.219 --> 01:22:56.179
You're just a bureaucrat!


01:22:56.263 --> 01:22:58.681
Better have good news for me.
Is he here?


01:22:58.766 --> 01:23:01.059
You think I need you to tell me
what the mission is?


01:23:01.143 --> 01:23:03.936
Yeah, I got it. Dunhill lighter.
I'll be there.


01:23:04.021 --> 01:23:05.688
And no one will be following me.


01:23:05.773 --> 01:23:07.565
Just make sure no one's following you.


01:23:07.650 --> 01:23:09.359
And how the hell
did the Russians find us?


01:23:09.443 --> 01:23:11.277
- What are you asking me for?
- Because you're communications!


01:23:11.362 --> 01:23:13.154
You're in charge of covering our tracks.


01:23:13.238 --> 01:23:16.032
You cannot afford to make mistakes
like that now, Benji.


01:23:16.116 --> 01:23:18.451
You're not a technician anymore.
You're a field agent.


01:23:18.535 --> 01:23:21.079
And you're just an "analyst."


01:23:21.163 --> 01:23:24.207
Right?


01:23:25.501 --> 01:23:27.543
Who are you really, Brandt?


01:23:29.213 --> 01:23:31.089
- What are you asking?
- What am I asking?


01:23:31.173 --> 01:23:32.924
Let me see if I can put it another way.


01:23:40.057 --> 01:23:44.268
How does an agent with skills like that
end up an analyst?


01:23:52.403 --> 01:23:54.612
Well, we all have our secrets.


01:23:56.115 --> 01:23:57.699
Don't we, Ethan?


01:24:02.621 --> 01:24:05.248
You tell me yours, I'll tell you mine.


01:24:24.977 --> 01:24:27.186
I have friends in the region.
Just sit tight.


01:24:27.271 --> 01:24:28.813
I'll send someone to get you out of here.


01:24:28.897 --> 01:24:30.064
What about Hendricks?
What's the plan?


01:24:30.149 --> 01:24:32.859
The plan was for us
to stop him together.


01:24:33.318 --> 01:24:35.445
Well, what are you going to do?


01:24:35.529 --> 01:24:36.571
Change the plan.


01:24:36.655 --> 01:24:38.865
Wait. That's it?


01:24:38.949 --> 01:24:41.868
What are you going to do,
go after him alone?


01:24:43.495 --> 01:24:46.581
Would you care to explain yourself,
Agent Brandt?


01:25:50.395 --> 01:25:53.481
I was on a protection detail in Croatia.


01:25:53.565 --> 01:25:56.651
Shadowing the assets,
husband and wife.


01:25:57.736 --> 01:25:59.612
They were never supposed to know
we were there.


01:25:59.696 --> 01:26:02.406
Whole thing's routine, it was a milk run.


01:26:05.077 --> 01:26:06.536
Three days in


01:26:07.746 --> 01:26:11.332
we caught wind that a Serbian hit squad
was after our couple.


01:26:11.416 --> 01:26:14.001
But my team had it under control.


01:26:14.086 --> 01:26:16.087
We knew they were coming.


01:26:16.672 --> 01:26:20.925
But I couldn't shake this feeling that I
should warn the couple somehow.


01:26:21.009 --> 01:26:23.386
I wanted to find a way to let them know.


01:26:25.764 --> 01:26:28.683
But, you know, orders are orders,
so I didn't.


01:26:33.605 --> 01:26:38.025
One day, the husband decides
to leave the hotel and go for a run,


01:26:38.110 --> 01:26:42.113
so I follow him,
and I leave two men with the wife.


01:26:43.657 --> 01:26:47.785
When I get back, my guys are
unconscious and the wife is gone.


01:26:49.705 --> 01:26:52.623
Local police found her body
three days later.


01:26:53.667 --> 01:26:55.585
What was left of her, anyway.


01:27:01.258 --> 01:27:03.634
That was my last day in the field.


01:27:04.678 --> 01:27:07.722
I couldn't face another
life-or-death situation after that.


01:27:07.806 --> 01:27:10.391
So what happened to the husband?


01:27:10.475 --> 01:27:11.642
I never saw him again.


01:27:13.562 --> 01:27:15.313
Until two days ago in Moscow,


01:27:15.397 --> 01:27:18.149
when the Secretary
introduced me to Ethan Hunt.


01:27:21.862 --> 01:27:25.323
No, that's not what happened.
She left him.


01:27:25.407 --> 01:27:28.159
Yeah, I heard that one, too, Benji.


01:27:28.660 --> 01:27:31.579
But, unfortunately, I was there.


01:27:32.998 --> 01:27:36.751
Just like I was there
when the Secretary got the phone call


01:27:36.835 --> 01:27:41.172
that Ethan was in custody for killing
six Serbian nationals in cold blood.


01:27:41.256 --> 01:27:42.423
An unsanctioned hit.


01:27:42.507 --> 01:27:43.466
Yeah.


01:27:43.550 --> 01:27:45.301
Disavowed.


01:27:54.019 --> 01:27:55.269
The next thing I know,


01:27:56.188 --> 01:27:58.189
I'm on a plane to Dubai,


01:27:59.858 --> 01:28:03.277
wondering the whole time, do I tell him?


01:28:05.530 --> 01:28:07.198
How do I tell him?


01:28:09.409 --> 01:28:11.202
That I'm responsible.


01:28:13.789 --> 01:28:14.956
I could have warned him.


01:28:15.040 --> 01:28:17.041
I should have warned him.


01:28:19.503 --> 01:28:20.962
But I didn't.


01:28:22.714 --> 01:28:24.173
And she died.


01:28:30.639 --> 01:28:34.308
Sergei! Sergei, my friend!


01:28:34.393 --> 01:28:37.436
I told you I would get him here.
Didn't I say?


01:28:37.521 --> 01:28:38.646
How do I know it's him?


01:28:38.730 --> 01:28:42.233
Yes, it's him.
You trust me, I trust you. Right?


01:28:42.734 --> 01:28:44.193
This is the guy!


01:28:44.277 --> 01:28:46.988
This is the guy, the one I told you about.


01:28:47.072 --> 01:28:49.615
So we can take these things off.


01:28:54.371 --> 01:28:57.248
Sorry. He's a great guy,
but he doesn't know you like I do.


01:28:57.332 --> 01:29:00.418
So, you work for
the American government.


01:29:01.795 --> 01:29:03.295
And you're an arms dealer.


01:29:03.380 --> 01:29:05.715
No, no, no. Sergei. Sergei.


01:29:06.299 --> 01:29:10.344
He's "independent
defense coordinator." Right?


01:29:11.555 --> 01:29:13.514
That you are. Very classy job.


01:29:13.598 --> 01:29:14.682
Listen. He's a friend.


01:29:14.766 --> 01:29:16.350
Those diamonds are for Bogdan.


01:29:16.435 --> 01:29:18.436
No, no. It's okay. You can have them.


01:29:18.520 --> 01:29:21.689
Whatever arrangements you made with
my cousin is between you and him.


01:29:21.773 --> 01:29:24.608
You want something from me, you pay.


01:29:24.693 --> 01:29:28.946
You misunderstand.
I'm not buying. I'm selling.


01:29:29.698 --> 01:29:31.866
You're selling.


01:29:31.950 --> 01:29:33.159
Selling what?


01:29:33.243 --> 01:29:34.618
The future.


01:29:34.703 --> 01:29:37.496
Yeah, I got all I need, thank you.


01:29:37.581 --> 01:29:39.248
Our countries are on the brink of war.


01:29:39.833 --> 01:29:41.709
War is very good for business.


01:29:41.793 --> 01:29:43.335
Nuclear war?


01:29:53.805 --> 01:29:54.889
Go on.


01:29:54.973 --> 01:29:56.932
I'm looking for a man
named Kurt Hendricks.


01:29:57.017 --> 01:29:58.642
You may know him as Cobalt.


01:29:58.727 --> 01:30:01.479
In either case,
I think you know what he wants.


01:30:01.563 --> 01:30:04.231
I'll bet he even tried
to buy it from you at some point.


01:30:05.650 --> 01:30:06.692
Go on.


01:30:06.777 --> 01:30:08.861
He has a case, he has codes.


01:30:09.613 --> 01:30:12.907
But they're worthless
without a tactical satellite.


01:30:12.991 --> 01:30:15.326
I want to know where he'd get it.


01:30:15.994 --> 01:30:19.497
A man with information like that
would be a potential terrorist.


01:30:20.415 --> 01:30:22.374
And to your government,


01:30:22.459 --> 01:30:26.545
a potential terrorist is a terrorist.


01:30:29.508 --> 01:30:30.508
If you help me,


01:30:31.843 --> 01:30:34.845
my friends become your friends.


01:30:37.974 --> 01:30:39.141
Sorry.


01:30:40.435 --> 01:30:42.103
I cannot help you.


01:30:47.609 --> 01:30:50.653
I certainly cannot tell you
that Russia quietly sold


01:30:50.737 --> 01:30:54.532
an obsolete tactical satellite
to a certain telecom in Mumbai.


01:30:56.368 --> 01:30:58.285
And whoever gave them that idea?


01:31:00.247 --> 01:31:02.164
An enterprising third party.


01:31:02.249 --> 01:31:03.749
Working on commission.


01:31:03.834 --> 01:31:07.086
Helping old friends. Making new ones.


01:31:07.754 --> 01:31:09.130
Can the satellite be shut down?


01:31:09.214 --> 01:31:11.132
That would take special skills,


01:31:12.050 --> 01:31:13.551
and you cannot do it alone.


01:31:39.911 --> 01:31:41.537
What's in the bags?


01:31:41.621 --> 01:31:42.997
It's our gear.


01:31:43.081 --> 01:31:44.874
How'd you get it?


01:31:44.958 --> 01:31:46.125
Made a friend.


01:31:47.252 --> 01:31:48.502
Well, I'm glad we could help.


01:31:48.587 --> 01:31:50.379
You could help now.


01:31:50.463 --> 01:31:52.339
Look, Ethan, before we...


01:31:52.424 --> 01:31:53.674
Whatever happened, happened.


01:31:54.217 --> 01:31:56.969
We still have a chance to clean this up,
but we have to do it now.


01:31:57.971 --> 01:32:00.181
And we have to do it together.


01:32:07.439 --> 01:32:08.814
Okay. So, where are we going?


01:32:10.567 --> 01:32:11.567
India.


01:32:15.071 --> 01:32:16.614
- India? India?
- Sure.


01:32:16.698 --> 01:32:17.781
Okay. Great.


01:32:21.453 --> 01:32:22.953
Love the jet.


01:32:23.663 --> 01:32:25.456
Wait till you see the car.


01:32:32.047 --> 01:32:33.088
Sidorov.


01:32:33.256 --> 01:32:34.798
How have you been, old friend?


01:32:34.966 --> 01:32:36.091
Oh, it's you.


01:32:37.052 --> 01:32:40.221
I've been busy with other things.


01:32:40.305 --> 01:32:42.264
But I'll be after you again soon enough.


01:32:44.809 --> 01:32:47.686
I understand you're looking for an American. ..


01:32:47.854 --> 01:32:48.854
I am.


01:32:49.981 --> 01:32:55.819
You're also looking for a nuclear launch device
stolen from the Kremlin two days ago.


01:32:56.279 --> 01:32:57.321
I am?


01:32:57.572 --> 01:32:59.865
I can help you find both.


01:33:00.825 --> 01:33:03.786
If... we can come to an understanding.


01:33:09.918 --> 01:33:11.126
Brij Nath.


01:33:11.211 --> 01:33:13.712
Brij Nath. Playboy. Multimedia tycoon.


01:33:13.797 --> 01:33:16.757
On the surface,
his entire network is state-of-the-art.


01:33:16.841 --> 01:33:18.759
But it's built on illegally acquired


01:33:18.843 --> 01:33:22.721
Cold War cast-offs, including this,
the Novosti satellite.


01:33:22.806 --> 01:33:24.598
Hendricks needs it
to launch a nuclear strike,


01:33:24.683 --> 01:33:27.184
and we have to shut it down
before he gets that chance.


01:33:27.269 --> 01:33:29.853
And to do that, we need to get
the access code from him.


01:33:29.938 --> 01:33:31.272
One way or another.


01:33:32.524 --> 01:33:34.066
And if I don't,


01:33:35.026 --> 01:33:36.568
none of this works.


01:33:37.862 --> 01:33:38.988
You can do this.


01:33:39.072 --> 01:33:40.197
Yeah.


01:33:41.032 --> 01:33:43.826
A week ago, I would have believed you.


01:33:49.040 --> 01:33:51.458
I don't blame you for what happened.


01:33:56.214 --> 01:33:59.883
She took someone you cared about.
That's not something you just


01:34:00.302 --> 01:34:01.302
let go.


01:34:03.054 --> 01:34:05.180
Did it make you feel better?


01:34:07.684 --> 01:34:10.602
When you killed the men
who killed your wife?


01:34:18.695 --> 01:34:20.571
We can't get them back.


01:34:26.953 --> 01:34:28.203
Okay, to shut down the satellite,


01:34:28.288 --> 01:34:31.081
we have to manually tap into
the central server.


01:34:31.166 --> 01:34:34.793
You'll enter through the exhaust vent,
wearing this under your suit.


01:34:34.878 --> 01:34:37.504
Drop down into the computer array,
and I'll catch you,


01:34:37.589 --> 01:34:40.924
then move you along the relay room
and you jack into the panel.


01:34:44.596 --> 01:34:47.181
Okay, so we enter the party
separately as guests.


01:34:47.265 --> 01:34:49.058
Ethan quarterbacks while Jane...


01:34:49.142 --> 01:34:50.642
Gets the codes from the billionaire.


01:34:50.727 --> 01:34:52.770
I switch off the fan,
you jump into the computer array,


01:34:52.854 --> 01:34:54.897
and I catch you,
you plug in the transmitter


01:34:54.981 --> 01:34:58.650
then Ethan feeds me the codes which I
then use to pinpoint Hendricks' location.


01:34:58.735 --> 01:35:01.904
Okay, but you just breezed over
something I think is really important.


01:35:01.988 --> 01:35:04.823
The computer array part, where I just...


01:35:05.867 --> 01:35:06.909
Jump?


01:35:07.744 --> 01:35:09.370
- And I catch you.
- Yeah.


01:35:09.454 --> 01:35:11.205
I don't. .. Why is that so hard to grasp?


01:35:11.873 --> 01:35:12.915
Well. ..


01:35:12.999 --> 01:35:17.711
Why? It's a 25-foot drop.
And we're using magnets.


01:35:17.796 --> 01:35:19.129
Yeah.


01:35:19.881 --> 01:35:22.966
In light of our recent efforts,
the technology's. ..


01:35:23.051 --> 01:35:25.010
The science is sound. All right?


01:35:25.095 --> 01:35:26.720
I'd be more worried about the heat.


01:35:28.014 --> 01:35:30.140
And then there's that. What heat?


01:35:30.934 --> 01:35:32.142
Well, it's like any computer, isn't it?


01:35:32.227 --> 01:35:35.229
If you switch off the fan,
it's gonna get really hot!


01:35:35.313 --> 01:35:36.397
Of course.


01:35:36.481 --> 01:35:38.107
Relatively, you know.


01:35:39.609 --> 01:35:43.112
Of course it will. So I'm jumping into a. ..


01:35:44.531 --> 01:35:47.491
An oven, essentially.


01:35:48.118 --> 01:35:49.785
Yeah. Essentially.


01:35:50.120 --> 01:35:52.287
But I'll catch you.


01:35:54.165 --> 01:35:55.332
Great.


01:36:24.028 --> 01:36:26.530
Aapka swagat hai, sir. Welcome, sir.


01:37:18.208 --> 01:37:19.583
Comm check.


01:37:20.251 --> 01:37:22.961
Saturn's got your five-by-five, Jupiter.


01:37:24.589 --> 01:37:26.089
This is Pluto.


01:37:28.259 --> 01:37:30.344
I have arrived at the party.


01:37:33.765 --> 01:37:34.765
There he is.


01:37:46.986 --> 01:37:48.612
Get us that code.


01:37:57.288 --> 01:37:59.081
Venus moving in on target.


01:38:10.927 --> 01:38:12.261
Hook's in.


01:38:14.305 --> 01:38:16.306
You do make an impression.


01:38:20.311 --> 01:38:21.311
Why am I Pluto?


01:38:21.396 --> 01:38:23.230
It's not even a planet anymore.


01:38:23.314 --> 01:38:25.065
Well, I think Uranus is available.


01:38:25.149 --> 01:38:27.442
It's funny 'cause you said "anus."


01:38:41.833 --> 01:38:42.833
I'm in position.


01:38:43.418 --> 01:38:45.210
Sending in the Rover.


01:38:49.841 --> 01:38:51.049
He's moving to you.


01:38:51.134 --> 01:38:52.843
Give him your back.


01:38:53.720 --> 01:38:55.345
Don't want to make it too easy for him.


01:38:55.430 --> 01:38:56.930
Are you gonna be talking
the whole time?


01:38:58.099 --> 01:39:01.476
In 20 minutes, I want a glass of
Cuvée Louis in every guest's hand.


01:39:01.561 --> 01:39:04.563
And make sure all of them have a bottle
to take home by the end of the night.


01:39:04.647 --> 01:39:05.731
Sure.


01:39:09.360 --> 01:39:10.569
Impressed yet?


01:39:11.863 --> 01:39:13.405
I'm more of a bourbon girl.


01:39:19.579 --> 01:39:20.704
I'm Brij Nath.


01:39:21.205 --> 01:39:23.248
Welcome to my humble home.


01:39:45.813 --> 01:39:47.397
And Rover's in position.


01:39:48.733 --> 01:39:49.941
Spinning down the turbine.


01:39:58.117 --> 01:39:59.117
He's e-mailing.


01:39:59.827 --> 01:40:01.328
Venus. Be Venus.


01:40:01.412 --> 01:40:02.746
Be Venus.


01:40:11.047 --> 01:40:12.255
Husband?


01:40:12.924 --> 01:40:13.924
Boyfriend?


01:40:14.967 --> 01:40:16.301
More of a


01:40:17.220 --> 01:40:18.261
co-worker.


01:40:19.055 --> 01:40:21.056
Saturn, take the leap.


01:40:25.645 --> 01:40:26.770
Okay.


01:40:30.733 --> 01:40:32.192
Jumping.


01:40:32.276 --> 01:40:33.944
Jumping now.


01:40:36.322 --> 01:40:37.322
Jump now?


01:40:37.407 --> 01:40:39.449
Yes. Commit. Jump.


01:40:39.742 --> 01:40:41.410
- Jump.
- Jump.


01:40:41.494 --> 01:40:43.412
- And I catch you.
- Now.


01:40:46.958 --> 01:40:50.085
So, you're sure
about this suit, right, Benji?


01:40:50.169 --> 01:40:51.211
Pretty sure.


01:40:51.963 --> 01:40:54.756
Now you're pretty sure?


01:40:55.842 --> 01:40:56.842
Jump.


01:40:57.969 --> 01:41:00.137
Oh, God. All right.


01:41:01.139 --> 01:41:02.139
Jump.


01:41:03.558 --> 01:41:04.599
Jump!


01:41:22.702 --> 01:41:25.203
Jupiter, he's gone.


01:41:29.709 --> 01:41:30.709
Did you jump?


01:41:30.793 --> 01:41:32.669
Should I not have jumped?


01:41:33.671 --> 01:41:34.671
'Cause I jumped!


01:41:36.966 --> 01:41:38.258
Stand by.


01:41:46.267 --> 01:41:47.768
I'm playing a hunch.


01:41:48.853 --> 01:41:50.312
Don't hit me.


01:42:07.705 --> 01:42:08.747
Hello?


01:42:08.831 --> 01:42:10.582
My God, you are


01:42:10.666 --> 01:42:12.793
a passionate creature.


01:42:14.712 --> 01:42:17.672
I would like to show you
my collection of art.


01:42:18.341 --> 01:42:20.175
I was waiting for you to ask.


01:42:20.259 --> 01:42:22.010
Then you have to find me.


01:42:22.094 --> 01:42:23.303
You're on.


01:42:23.387 --> 01:42:25.555
I'm heading upstairs.


01:42:43.366 --> 01:42:44.866
All right, now be careful,


01:42:44.951 --> 01:42:47.160
because it's probably getting a bit hot.


01:42:47.245 --> 01:42:49.579
We have to get to that satellite
before Hendricks does.


01:43:04.595 --> 01:43:07.347
Look left. Look up.


01:43:07.431 --> 01:43:10.100
I find your capricious passion intriguing.


01:43:11.435 --> 01:43:13.603
Let me tell you one thing.
He's not your type.


01:43:13.688 --> 01:43:16.940
Completely not your type.
He's completely cold. I'm hot.


01:43:19.026 --> 01:43:21.486
Like all Indian men, I'm very hot.


01:43:21.571 --> 01:43:22.529
Eight o'clock.


01:43:22.613 --> 01:43:23.613
Hot! Very hot.


01:43:23.698 --> 01:43:25.532
He's at your eight o'clock.


01:43:25.616 --> 01:43:27.951
As you move towards me,
you're getting hotter.


01:43:28.953 --> 01:43:31.872
Whoa. Up, up! Up, up!


01:43:31.956 --> 01:43:34.416
Too much, too much, too much!


01:43:38.963 --> 01:43:40.297
I see you.


01:43:42.008 --> 01:43:45.552
I'd heard you have one of the finest
private collections in the world.


01:43:45.636 --> 01:43:48.221
Well, at the very least, it's private.


01:44:07.325 --> 01:44:09.284
Saturn? How we doing
in the relay room?


01:44:09.368 --> 01:44:10.368
In position.


01:44:12.747 --> 01:44:14.080
I see the satellite.


01:44:20.880 --> 01:44:22.130
Can I help you, gentlemen?


01:44:22.214 --> 01:44:23.798
I don't think so.


01:44:30.181 --> 01:44:31.681
Need those codes, guys.


01:44:40.566 --> 01:44:43.568
All originals from Chhatarpur District.


01:44:46.906 --> 01:44:49.115
You know, the Tantrics believe


01:44:50.701 --> 01:44:55.455
that the Swadhisthana chakra hides
our most subconscious of desires.


01:45:47.425 --> 01:45:51.344
Uplink to satellite.
Reboot to original military specs.


01:45:51.679 --> 01:45:53.430
Download the virus.


01:46:01.272 --> 01:46:05.525
What the hell is that?


01:46:05.609 --> 01:46:06.568
What the hell is what?


01:46:06.652 --> 01:46:08.028
It's going haywire!


01:46:08.112 --> 01:46:10.030
It's downloaded a virus
from the satellite.


01:46:10.114 --> 01:46:11.322
Hendricks is killing the server


01:46:11.407 --> 01:46:13.033
before we can kill the satellite.


01:46:13.117 --> 01:46:15.201
Hendricks is reprogramming
the satellite.


01:46:15.286 --> 01:46:18.371
He's gonna have launch
capability in five minutes!


01:46:18.456 --> 01:46:20.415
- Something wrong?
- No.


01:46:21.083 --> 01:46:23.251
Jane, you gotta move.
We need that code.


01:46:23.335 --> 01:46:25.211
Finally we're alone.


01:46:32.970 --> 01:46:35.388
Venus, now's the time. Kick his ass


01:46:35.473 --> 01:46:37.140
and get the code.


01:46:37.475 --> 01:46:40.643
We are alone, aren't we?


01:46:41.312 --> 01:46:43.980
No one will interrupt us.


01:46:48.319 --> 01:46:49.986
Move and I break your neck.


01:46:50.071 --> 01:46:52.655
The override sequence
for the relay station.


01:46:52.740 --> 01:46:55.033
Say it now or never speak again.


01:46:56.035 --> 01:46:57.243
The codes.


01:46:58.496 --> 01:47:00.789
46, 82,


01:47:01.665 --> 01:47:03.166
93.


01:47:06.087 --> 01:47:07.087
Benji, what happened?


01:47:07.171 --> 01:47:08.922
The system's crashed! We're too late.


01:47:09.006 --> 01:47:10.632
No, no, no. He's revealed himself.


01:47:10.716 --> 01:47:12.342
Benji, can you pinpoint
Hendricks' location?


01:47:13.552 --> 01:47:15.595
Hendricks is signaling out of a state-run


01:47:15.679 --> 01:47:17.555
TV station 6.7 miles from here.


01:47:17.640 --> 01:47:18.681
Send me the coordinates.


01:47:18.766 --> 01:47:20.433
Good work, Brandt.
Now get the hell out of there.


01:47:20.518 --> 01:47:21.601
Back me up!


01:47:21.685 --> 01:47:23.770
Jane, tie it off with Nath
and meet me at the rally point.


01:47:29.693 --> 01:47:30.693
Sleep tight


01:47:32.029 --> 01:47:33.905
Faster, Benji! Just straight through!


01:47:38.035 --> 01:47:39.410
Wait! Stop!


01:47:39.495 --> 01:47:40.995
Take me through!


01:47:41.080 --> 01:47:44.082
It's not responding! A little bit of
patience would be appreciated!


01:47:59.765 --> 01:48:01.641
I can't reach the top!


01:48:03.561 --> 01:48:05.436
More fan! More fan!


01:48:05.521 --> 01:48:06.896
More fan!


01:48:06.981 --> 01:48:08.857
There's nothing I can do! It's maxed out!


01:48:26.250 --> 01:48:28.751
Brandt?


01:48:30.296 --> 01:48:33.631
Next time, I get to seduce the rich guy.


01:48:44.435 --> 01:48:46.686
Satellite weaponized and online.


01:48:46.770 --> 01:48:49.147
Upload the new authentication codes.


01:48:49.231 --> 01:48:51.191
Lock Russian Central Command
out of the system.


01:48:51.609 --> 01:48:53.026
Isolate the sub.


01:48:53.110 --> 01:48:57.780
We'll fire just one missile,
an apparent retaliation for the Kremlin.


01:48:58.282 --> 01:49:00.074
That should start the ball rolling.


01:49:00.159 --> 01:49:01.242
I'm here, Ethan.


01:49:01.327 --> 01:49:03.411
How long until Hendricks
can launch a missile?


01:49:04.455 --> 01:49:05.705
Less than 30 seconds!


01:49:07.499 --> 01:49:09.375
We need another route.


01:49:10.461 --> 01:49:12.128
Turn left up ahead,
take the alley on the right.


01:49:27.394 --> 01:49:28.394
We have uplink.


01:49:39.114 --> 01:49:41.699
Ethan, Hendricks
has started the launch sequence.


01:49:41.784 --> 01:49:43.451
How much time until missiles are flying?


01:49:43.535 --> 01:49:44.786
Three minutes!


01:49:48.540 --> 01:49:50.041
We're three and a half minutes out.


01:49:53.504 --> 01:49:57.340
We can make it.


01:50:03.931 --> 01:50:04.931
Captain...


01:50:09.728 --> 01:50:12.230
Connect to Central Command for launch verification.


01:50:12.314 --> 01:50:13.314
Right away.


01:50:15.192 --> 01:50:17.902
Proceed with Operation "Iron Fist".


01:50:18.070 --> 01:50:19.862
Command to Launch is confirmed.


01:50:20.239 --> 01:50:22.198
Cease all further communication.


01:50:22.366 --> 01:50:23.366
Over and out.


01:50:25.786 --> 01:50:26.995
Next left.


01:50:40.467 --> 01:50:41.467
Proceed.


01:51:02.781 --> 01:51:04.991
Ethan? We're too late.


01:51:05.075 --> 01:51:07.076
The missile's in the air.


01:51:19.465 --> 01:51:21.215
There has to be a way
to abort the warhead.


01:51:21.300 --> 01:51:23.051
If there is one,
it'll be on the launch device.


01:51:23.135 --> 01:51:24.510
We're gonna get that case.


01:51:35.189 --> 01:51:37.774
May there be peace on Earth.


01:51:42.780 --> 01:51:44.405
Disable the relay.


01:51:45.783 --> 01:51:47.867
Get Wistrom! Inside, inside!


01:52:22.361 --> 01:52:24.237
Wistrom destroyed the relay.


01:52:24.321 --> 01:52:25.530
Ethan went after Hendricks
and the case, but...


01:52:25.614 --> 01:52:27.824
Doesn't matter if he has the case.
We can't transmit the abort codes.


01:52:28.158 --> 01:52:29.117
Can you fix it?


01:52:29.201 --> 01:52:31.911
Yeah... It's gonna be pointless
if we don't have any power.


01:52:31.995 --> 01:52:32.995
Wistrom!


01:52:35.082 --> 01:52:36.749
- Jane!
- I'm okay.


01:52:38.502 --> 01:52:40.795
No, you are not okay. She's hit.


01:52:41.213 --> 01:52:42.797
You stay here and cover Benji.


01:52:42.881 --> 01:52:45.883
Benji, get this thing rewired
and back online. I'll get the power on.


01:52:45.968 --> 01:52:47.510
We can do this.


01:56:01.913 --> 01:56:04.707
I'm taking that briefcase!


01:56:08.253 --> 01:56:09.754
No! No!


01:56:57.052 --> 01:56:58.511
He's been gone too long.


01:56:58.595 --> 01:57:00.054
Damn it! Listen.


01:57:00.138 --> 01:57:03.099
When the power comes on,
these two drives go into this bay, okay?


01:57:47.102 --> 01:57:49.729
Mission accomplished!


01:58:31.188 --> 01:58:32.438
Don't touch him!


01:58:39.112 --> 01:58:40.946
This one is mine.


01:58:53.084 --> 01:58:55.878
So, we are not enemies.


01:58:57.798 --> 01:59:00.508
The phone call
from that arms dealer in Dubai.


01:59:00.801 --> 01:59:02.384
You wanted me to find you.


01:59:06.431 --> 01:59:08.474
How else to believe this?


01:59:16.107 --> 01:59:17.107
Hospital?


01:59:19.361 --> 01:59:21.445
And in other news, eight weeks later,


01:59:21.530 --> 01:59:23.113
the debate continues.


01:59:23.198 --> 01:59:27.535
Eyewitnesses remain adamant
that the object was some sort of aircraft,


01:59:27.619 --> 01:59:31.455
but officials with the Department of
Defense insist it was simply a meteor


01:59:31.540 --> 01:59:34.250
large enough to be
visible during daylight.


01:59:34.501 --> 01:59:36.418
You actually said that.


01:59:36.753 --> 01:59:38.045
Out loud.


01:59:38.672 --> 01:59:40.089
"Mission accomplished."


01:59:40.173 --> 01:59:41.215
I said it.


01:59:41.299 --> 01:59:43.843
You're still corny, Ethan.


01:59:43.927 --> 01:59:46.762
I can't imagine
the look on that guy's face.


01:59:48.557 --> 01:59:50.599
- Hey.
- This must be them.


01:59:50.684 --> 01:59:53.978
Luther Stickell,
the firm of Carter, Dunn and Brandt.


01:59:55.605 --> 01:59:59.441
I blew an entire weekend
on the bottom of the San Francisco Bay


02:00:00.569 --> 02:00:02.528
no thanks to you clowns.


02:00:04.865 --> 02:00:06.448
No, man, you know I got this.


02:00:07.450 --> 02:00:09.952
I know. I'll see you in Kandahar.


02:00:13.748 --> 02:00:15.875
Thanks for meeting me.


02:00:15.959 --> 02:00:18.252
So, I hear the insurance
company's refusing


02:00:18.336 --> 02:00:20.546
to pay the claim
on that car you crashed, Ethan.


02:00:20.630 --> 02:00:24.258
Something about intentional 100-meter
vertical drops not being covered.


02:00:24.342 --> 02:00:25.509
Go figure.


02:00:29.097 --> 02:00:30.723
How's the leg?


02:00:30.807 --> 02:00:32.057
Still working.


02:00:32.976 --> 02:00:34.018
You?


02:00:34.436 --> 02:00:35.644
Healing.


02:00:37.522 --> 02:00:38.689
I'm fine, by the way.


02:00:40.025 --> 02:00:41.692
I mean, I'm not actually sleeping, per se.


02:00:41.985 --> 02:00:44.820
You know. Cold sweats.
Middle of the night.


02:00:46.489 --> 02:00:49.074
All these people
are just happy and smiling


02:00:49.159 --> 02:00:50.910
and they are completely
oblivious to the fact


02:00:50.994 --> 02:00:53.078
that they were almost vaporized.


02:00:54.164 --> 02:00:55.789
And if it hadn't been for. ..


02:00:55.874 --> 02:00:57.207
Dumb luck?


02:00:57.667 --> 02:00:58.667
Was it?


02:01:00.128 --> 02:01:03.631
I mean, look,
we were unprepared, in the dark.


02:01:04.132 --> 02:01:05.466
Disavowed.


02:01:06.676 --> 02:01:08.469
And the only thing
that functioned properly


02:01:09.387 --> 02:01:10.930
on that mission


02:01:11.848 --> 02:01:13.349
was this team.


02:01:15.435 --> 02:01:18.020
I don't know how we ended up together,


02:01:19.814 --> 02:01:21.231
but I'm glad we did.


02:01:28.698 --> 02:01:29.907
Your missions.


02:01:30.867 --> 02:01:32.701
Choose to accept them.


02:01:38.291 --> 02:01:39.959
Hey, look, I'm in.


02:01:40.335 --> 02:01:41.919
Seriously. It's not as if any mission


02:01:42.003 --> 02:01:44.129
is gonna be rougher
than the last one, is it?


02:01:45.548 --> 02:01:46.799
I mean, that's just...


02:01:46.883 --> 02:01:48.550
Bomb. .. Is it?


02:02:06.903 --> 02:02:08.237
Thanks, Ethan.


02:02:08.571 --> 02:02:09.738
Thank you.


02:02:11.741 --> 02:02:12.741
Agent Hunt.


02:02:12.826 --> 02:02:14.201
Agent Carter.


02:02:22.794 --> 02:02:23.836
Brandt.


02:02:27.507 --> 02:02:29.008
I'm not picking up that phone, Ethan,


02:02:29.092 --> 02:02:31.719
because I don't think
you want me in the field.


02:02:34.681 --> 02:02:36.640
I know your wife is dead.


02:02:38.810 --> 02:02:41.020
I was there in Croatia.


02:02:42.772 --> 02:02:44.231
I was there for one reason.


02:02:44.315 --> 02:02:45.482
One.


02:02:46.276 --> 02:02:47.735
And I failed.


02:02:52.282 --> 02:02:53.866
It was my job to protect her.


02:02:54.576 --> 02:02:56.035
How do you know she's dead?


02:02:59.414 --> 02:03:00.456
There was a body.


02:03:00.957 --> 02:03:02.166
Did you see it?


02:03:05.879 --> 02:03:07.921
You killed those Serbians.


02:03:08.006 --> 02:03:09.048
I had to get her back.


02:03:09.132 --> 02:03:10.716
You were sent to Rankow Prison.


02:03:10.800 --> 02:03:12.593
That was a sacrifice
I was willing to make.


02:03:12.677 --> 02:03:15.471
IMF suspected Hendricks
had people in Rankow.


02:03:18.183 --> 02:03:20.809
And six dead Serbians
was the ideal cover.


02:03:22.687 --> 02:03:24.521
Waste not, want not.


02:03:41.539 --> 02:03:43.665
The Secretary never told me.


02:03:46.961 --> 02:03:50.798
I accepted the Rankow Prison mission
on one condition:


02:03:50.882 --> 02:03:53.092
That no one could know
she was still alive.


02:03:54.677 --> 02:03:56.970
But you're telling me.


02:04:05.021 --> 02:04:07.606
When did you find out
that I was in Croatia?


02:04:08.274 --> 02:04:10.234
I pulled your file after India.


02:04:11.111 --> 02:04:12.319
Right.


02:04:14.280 --> 02:04:16.824
So you had to fake your wife's death.


02:04:17.659 --> 02:04:21.036
As long as we were together,
she could never be safe.


02:04:21.996 --> 02:04:24.790
It wasn't your job to protect her, Brandt.


02:04:27.293 --> 02:04:28.544
It's mine.


02:04:30.713 --> 02:04:31.839
Okay.


02:04:35.802 --> 02:04:37.052
So we're good.


02:04:38.388 --> 02:04:39.721
We're good.


02:05:39.449 --> 02:05:41.200
Come on!


02:06:01.221 --> 02:06:02.304
Good evening, Mr. Hunt.


02:06:02.388 --> 02:06:06.683
36 hours ago, there was a breach
in our military's communication network.


02:06:06.809 --> 02:06:10.270
Now, an emerging terror
organization known as The Syndicate


02:06:10.355 --> 02:06:14.024
has control of our entire drone fleet.
Their targets: Unknown.


02:06:14.317 --> 02:06:17.027
Your mission,
should you choose to accept it...
